00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:44,140
Now, I'll look into
getting you new uniforms.

266
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:47,077
I'm sorry, sir, but we have other duties.

267
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:48,160
I'm a nobleman.

268
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,986
That means I get what I want.

269
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:53,337
Don't worry, I'll have a
word with your superiors.

270
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:54,250
Yes, sir.

271
00:17:57,340 --> 00:17:59,900
Listen, Sabo, it's not too late for you.

272
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:03,957
From now on, you'll lock yourself in
your room and learn to be a proper noble.

273
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:04,870
No!

274
00:18:04,953 --> 00:18:06,291
I don't want to be cruel,

275
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:10,340
but I am certainly capable of it
and anything else I so desire.

276
00:18:10,620 --> 00:18:13,560
You could disappear,
just like your friends.

277
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:16,440
Are we clear?

278
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:19,380
I think so.

279
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:24,500
Ace. Luffy.

280
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:33,100
If Stella can study hard, then so can you.

281
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,165
Everything will work out fine.

282
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,517
And then your parents,

283
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:41,797
who work so hard to build a proper
future for you, can finally be happy.

284
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:42,998
Won't that be nice?

285
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:47,220
I'm sure it'll be nice for you as well.

286
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:49,780
Just give it some time.

287
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:53,310
Papa!

288
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,980
If you're sad, I can help.

289
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:02,467
Dependable as always, Stella.

290
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:05,397
We've got that big ceremony
coming up, you know.

291
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:07,304
Let's buy you some new clothes.

292
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:10,722
You'll look so handsome
for the Celestial Dragon.

293
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:22,841
Study hard, and I'll check
your homework tomorrow.

294
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:24,940
Have a pleasant afternoon.

295
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,920
Don't worry, guys.

296
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,200
I'm fine.

297
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,060
And you're tough.

298
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,480
So I know you're okay, too.

299
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,840
There's no way you died in that fire.

300
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:59,460
I just wish I could see you, even once.

301
00:20:02,020 --> 00:20:03,600
But if people follow me,

302
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:07,642
they'll find out you're still alive
and you'll be in danger again.

303
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:13,120
It looks nice from the outside,
but this house is a birdcage.

304
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:17,752
I'm going to lose my mind if I have to
stay in this stuffy, stuck-up place.

305
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:27,340
I thought I found freedom, but
it seems to keep slipping away.

306
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,820
All right, we're off.

307
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,840
Take good care of Sabo.

308
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:39,260
We won't be back until
late. Yes, sir. As you wish.

309
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:00,720
After much anticipation,

310
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:05,480
the day of the World Nobles' visit
to the Goa Kingdom arrives at last.

311
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:10,740
A lavish ceremony is prepared to greet
his ship as it enters the harbor.

312
00:21:17,180 --> 00:21:18,180
Hey, wait!

313
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,680
Is that a ship leaving port?

314
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:22,440
A what? What?

315
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:23,520
A fishing boat?

316
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:26,730
Hey!

317
00:21:26,813 --> 00:21:27,643
Come back!

318
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,940
You're blocking their path!

319
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:32,760
Why, it's just a child.

320
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:35,200
A little boy is steering that boat.

321
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:36,820
Then he's a noble?

322
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:39,377
But surely all the
families are here watching.

323
00:21:39,460 --> 00:21:40,640
It can't be.

324
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,420
Nice weather today.

325
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,459
It's just perfect for setting sail.

326
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:55,420
Uh, crap! That's mine! It was stolen!

327
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:57,838
I have nothing to do with this mess!

328
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:58,900
His flag!

329
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,797
He's got a Jolly Roger on it.

330
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:03,292
Is he trying to be a pirate or something?

331
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,540
Does it matter?

332
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:06,777
The kid's flag isn't the issue here.

333
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:08,857
He's heading straight for the ship.

334
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:11,257
The Celestial Dragon
isn't gonna like this.

335
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:13,737
Either you lose that boat
or you lose your job!

336
00:22:13,820 --> 00:22:14,650
Do you hear me?

337
00:22:14,733 --> 00:22:15,563
Fix it now!

338
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:16,890
Uh, yes, sir.

339
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:18,250
Hey!

340
00:22:19,540 --> 00:22:22,520
Get back here, kid! Are you nuts?

341
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:27,525
I'm not afraid of anything
as long as I'm free.

342
00:22:27,660 --> 00:22:29,836
I just have to be far away from here.

343
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:32,220
I have to follow my own dream.

344
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:38,291
Nobody's gonna change me.

345
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:41,350
Huh?

346
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:43,560
Holy crap, Sabo.

347
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:46,072
What do you think you're doing out there?

348
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:49,800
Give them a warm welcome, everyone!

349
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:11,520
Wow, that's one big ship.

350
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:13,822
It could run right over me easy.

351
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:17,020
Let's avoid that, shall we?

352
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:23,220
This is a first for me!

353
00:23:23,460 --> 00:23:26,237
The Celestial Dragons hardly
ever make visits like this!

354
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:27,980
I hope nobody mucks this up!

355
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:30,688
We didn't burn all those
people for nothing!

356
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:33,340
What is that wretched little thing?

357
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:36,859
It seems to be a fishing boat, sir.

358
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:42,497
That's so cool!

359
00:23:42,580 --> 00:23:45,874
I hope I'm the captain of a
big ship like that some day.

360
00:24:01,740 --> 00:24:02,920
Get out of my way!

361
00:24:03,060 --> 00:24:04,120
I gotta find eggs!

362
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:05,740
Easy, Luffy, easy.

363
00:24:06,140 --> 00:24:09,081
I know how you feel, but
it's still too dangerous.

364
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:13,137
You got banged up pretty bad and
the place is crawling with soldiers.

365
00:24:13,220 --> 00:24:14,050
Who cares?

366
00:24:14,133 --> 00:24:15,980
Please come down and listen to me.

367
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:17,200
We get it.

368
00:24:18,100 --> 00:24:19,320
We're scared too.

369
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:24,017
But right now, we just need to have faith
that the boss and ace are still alive.

370
00:24:24,100 --> 00:24:26,924
Tiger went back to look
for him, so be patient.

371
00:24:28,620 --> 00:24:29,450
Understand?

372
00:24:29,533 --> 00:24:31,800
This is hard on everyone, OK?

373
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,520
The fishing boat has been hit.

374
00:24:37,860 --> 00:24:39,277
What happened to the child?

375
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:42,097
That kid shouldn't have gotten
in the Celestial Dragon's way!

376
00:24:42,180 --> 00:24:43,560
Get out of there!

377
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:45,330
Damn!

378
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:48,800
Why'd he shoot at me?

379
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:50,710
St.

380
00:24:50,793 --> 00:24:52,756
Jalmec, there's a child on that ship!

381
00:24:52,920 --> 00:24:55,757
Anyone who flies a black
flag is a filthy pirate.

382
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:57,134
His age is irrelevant.

383
00:24:57,540 --> 00:24:58,900
He must pay.

384
00:25:04,100 --> 00:25:05,100
Come on!

385
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:06,977
A commoner should know better.

386
00:25:07,060 --> 00:25:09,900
Don't cross my ship,
you stupid pirate brat!

387
00:25:23,220 --> 00:25:24,050
What?

388
00:25:24,133 --> 00:25:25,917
Why would they fire on
that ship a second time?

389
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:26,830
Who cares?

390
00:25:26,913 --> 00:25:28,517
We don't want to make
the celestial dragon mad.

391
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:29,957
This is an important ceremony.

392
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:31,746
Let him do whatever he wants.

393
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:33,940
Clear the wreckage already!

394
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,300
Hey, I got news.

395
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:00,817
Ace and the boss are...

396
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:01,780
What is it?

397
00:26:02,820 --> 00:26:03,760
They came back.

398
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,080
They both made it.

399
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:29,917
I was...

400
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,280
so scared.

401
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:32,696
She's badly wounded.

402
00:26:32,940 --> 00:26:34,157
Get them both inside.

403
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,070
Now!

404
00:26:35,153 --> 00:26:35,983
Hurry!

405
00:26:36,066 --> 00:26:37,420
Hang in there, boss.

406
00:26:40,300 --> 00:26:41,130
Ace!

407
00:26:41,460 --> 00:26:42,520
Get off!

408
00:26:44,840 --> 00:26:45,820
Come on.

409
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:47,999
Did you seriously think I was dead?

410
00:26:48,460 --> 00:26:49,290
Baby!

411
00:26:49,373 --> 00:26:50,456
Quit crying already!

412
00:26:51,820 --> 00:26:54,291
I'm standing right in front of you, dummy!

413
00:26:54,380 --> 00:26:55,280
Come on, Ace.

414
00:26:55,420 --> 00:26:57,479
Take it easy on the kiddo for once.

415
00:26:57,700 --> 00:26:59,465
Luffy's just happy to see you.

416
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:07,357
What happened the night of the fire?

417
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:10,797
We all came back here with Luffy,
so we haven't heard a word.

418
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:14,468
Can you tell us everything that
happened to you and the boss?

419
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:15,490
Oh.

420
00:27:15,573 --> 00:27:17,620
Well, um, we fought Blue Jam.

421
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,700
We barely defeated him.

422
00:27:25,620 --> 00:27:28,973
And we tried to catch up to
you guys as fast as we could.

423
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:31,280
But the fire was blocking our way.

424
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,717
We made it through the fire.

425
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:36,859
Dadan was suffering from
some serious burns, though.

426
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:41,395
Eventually, we managed to get to the
riverside in the In-Between Forest.

427
00:27:45,180 --> 00:27:49,297
I went into town to steal medicine
and grab whatever food I could find.

428
00:27:49,380 --> 00:27:53,080
I'm no doctor, but I did what
I could to save Dedan's life.

429
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:01,157
What an ordeal!

430
00:28:01,240 --> 00:28:05,740
In any case, all that matters is that
both of you are back safe. I'm sorry.

431
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:07,000
I made you worry.

432
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:11,353
That fire was huge, and they
were hunting down survivors.

433
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:13,856
Sabo must think we're dead right now.

434
00:28:17,380 --> 00:28:21,520
This kingdom's likely full of lowly
plebeians that will get in my way.

435
00:28:21,860 --> 00:28:23,697
Be on the lookout for any disruption.

436
00:28:23,780 --> 00:28:24,610
Right.

437
00:28:29,860 --> 00:28:31,840
I wonder what Sava's been up to.

438
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:34,877
But at least Ace finally
made it back, right?

439
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:37,136
He even carried Dadan home with them.

440
00:28:38,580 --> 00:28:41,340
Ace, when I came for you...

441
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:42,800
I'm staying!

442
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:43,940
I won't run.

443
00:28:45,900 --> 00:28:47,600
Why did you do that?

444
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:48,940
I don't know.

445
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:51,005
I can't help but get fired up.

446
00:28:51,660 --> 00:28:55,778
I'm afraid if I run, that I might
leave something important behind me.

447
00:28:55,980 --> 00:28:56,940
So I fight.

448
00:28:59,580 --> 00:29:02,820
Luffy was there, so I had no choice.

449
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:06,346
It's tough to explain,
but I think that's why.

450
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:13,235
Even when he faced a wave of
far more powerful enemies,

451
00:29:14,480 --> 00:29:16,777
Roger would never think of running away.

452
00:29:16,860 --> 00:29:18,457
Did that fool have a death wish?

453
00:29:18,540 --> 00:29:19,817
Running away is a strategy too.

454
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:23,100
For him, it wasn't even
an option. Think about it.

455
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:25,437
Retreat means leaving people behind.

456
00:29:25,520 --> 00:29:29,477
If Roger ran, he'd be abandoning
his crew, the people he loved most.

457
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:33,020
So when you think about it,
it's not that he wouldn't run.

458
00:29:33,340 --> 00:29:36,517
Rather, he made sure the enemy
couldn't go after his crew.

459
00:29:36,600 --> 00:29:38,180
He always protected them.

460
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:41,197
He was a different kind of
animal in times like those.

461
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:43,597
He once wrecked a whole
country's army because

462
00:29:43,680 --> 00:29:46,097
some soldiers decided to
mouth off about his men.

463
00:29:46,180 --> 00:29:48,820
When he was angry,
Roger would get violent.

464
00:29:49,140 --> 00:29:53,316
He was selfish and short-tempered,
but he wore his heart on his sleeve.

465
00:29:53,580 --> 00:29:55,756
He was like a boy that never grew up.

466
00:29:55,940 --> 00:29:59,175
For better or worse, his
childhood was a lot like Aces.

467
00:29:59,580 --> 00:30:04,051
The pain he went through just made him
hold on tighter to the ones he loved.

468
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:12,087
Roger could be a very reckless man, but
he lived to become king of the pirates.

469
00:30:12,280 --> 00:30:13,260
No easy feat.

470
00:30:14,060 --> 00:30:18,766
Despite his flaws and his bad reputation,
his crew still trusted him completely.

471
00:30:19,360 --> 00:30:23,860
Sure, I may be a marine, but
even I can't help respecting him!

472
00:30:25,280 --> 00:30:27,637
That's why I decided to take care of Ace.

473
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:30,120
I'm the one taking care of him, you ass!

474
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:33,329
Do you got something
you want to say to me?

475
00:30:33,520 --> 00:30:34,660
No, never mind.

476
00:30:36,040 --> 00:30:38,537
People all over the
world still hate Roger!

477
00:30:38,620 --> 00:30:41,417
And even though Ace holds
a grudge against him too?

478
00:30:41,500 --> 00:30:44,300
They really are like father, like son.

479
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:47,560
All right, wonder who's gonna win?

480
00:30:48,980 --> 00:30:49,810
Dogra!

481
00:30:51,340 --> 00:30:54,164
You went to town to look
for Asa to dawn, right?

482
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:56,595
Surprise, they came back home already!

483
00:30:56,780 --> 00:30:57,960
Did they really?

484
00:30:58,300 --> 00:31:00,460
That's just great. Perfect.

485
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:03,177
What? Sabo?

486
00:31:03,260 --> 00:31:04,420
That can't be.

487
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:07,500
You're lying to me, dammit!

488
00:31:07,820 --> 00:31:09,677
Why would you even joke
about that kind of thing?

489
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:10,590
Take it easy!

490
00:31:10,673 --> 00:31:13,260
I told you exactly what I saw, I swear.

491
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:14,737
I know how you feel.

492
00:31:14,820 --> 00:31:17,557
Everything happened so fast,
I could hardly believe it.

493
00:31:17,640 --> 00:31:21,557
It felt like a nightmare, but
I know that was Sabo. Shut up.

494
00:31:21,640 --> 00:31:24,397
We watched him go back with his
dad to their home in Hightown.

495
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:26,637
You can't have seen him
out at sea by himself.

496
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:27,550
That's right.

497
00:31:27,633 --> 00:31:28,777
Sabo is with his family.

498
00:31:28,860 --> 00:31:30,857
And it's like us know how he feels.

499
00:31:30,940 --> 00:31:34,960
We know what it means to be turned
away from your home, to be free.

500
00:31:35,580 --> 00:31:37,317
Sabo didn't want to be a noble.

501
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:40,800
If he was truly happy, he
wouldn't have gone out to sea.

502
00:31:41,100 --> 00:31:44,777
And the Sabo I saw wasn't just
sailing away from his family.

503
00:31:44,860 --> 00:31:46,720
He was flying a Jolly Roger.

504
00:31:58,540 --> 00:32:00,246
We shouldn't have let him go.

505
00:32:00,360 --> 00:32:01,478
It's all our fault.

506
00:32:02,740 --> 00:32:05,260
Even if I had parents, I was still alone.

507
00:32:07,280 --> 00:32:10,377
Sabo, why didn't we go back into
town and bring him back here?

508
00:32:10,460 --> 00:32:11,401
We're so stupid.

509
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:14,417
Tell me where I can find
the bastard that killed him.

510
00:32:14,500 --> 00:32:16,417
I'm going to beat him to
death with my bare hands.

511
00:32:16,500 --> 00:32:17,897
You can't kill a celestial dragon.

512
00:32:17,980 --> 00:32:18,810
That's impossible.

513
00:32:18,893 --> 00:32:19,960
I'll make him pay.

514
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:22,060
Hold on, Ace.

515
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:25,562
Enough of that, you little punk.

516
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:32,697
You think you're so tough when you're
really just a cocky, stubborn little brat.

517
00:32:32,780 --> 00:32:34,897
What can you do against a world noble?

518
00:32:34,980 --> 00:32:36,577
You think he's just some thug?

519
00:32:36,660 --> 00:32:38,500
You're just some no-name kid.

520
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:40,697
You'll die and nobody will give a crap.

521
00:32:40,780 --> 00:32:42,617
Swept under the rug the very next day.

522
00:32:42,700 --> 00:32:45,357
It was this whole rotten
country that killed Sabo.

523
00:32:45,440 --> 00:32:46,580
This rotten world.

524
00:32:47,100 --> 00:32:49,747
What can a scrawny brat
like you do about it?

525
00:32:50,820 --> 00:32:53,937
Your father, on the other hand,
changed the world with his death.

526
00:32:54,020 --> 00:32:58,902
When you become a man as important as him,
then and only then can you take revenge.

527
00:33:02,540 --> 00:33:03,840
Tie this fool up.

528
00:33:04,980 --> 00:33:05,810
Yes, ma 'am.

529
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:08,390
Zappa!

530
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:11,790
Dammit!

531
00:33:13,980 --> 00:33:15,120
Shut up, Luffy!

532
00:33:15,380 --> 00:33:18,100
Quit crying like a girl
or else I'll... Ow!

533
00:33:34,380 --> 00:33:37,180
You've come to your senses now, I hope.

534
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:43,080
Guys, untie him. Right.

535
00:33:44,940 --> 00:33:46,377
Try to keep your cool, okay?

536
00:33:46,460 --> 00:33:47,520
Where's Luffy?

537
00:33:47,820 --> 00:33:49,137
He was crying all night.

538
00:33:49,220 --> 00:33:50,396
Finally fell asleep.

539
00:33:51,400 --> 00:33:52,960
Oh my gosh!

540
00:33:53,120 --> 00:33:54,657
You're not gonna believe this!

541
00:33:54,740 --> 00:33:55,960
We got a letter!

542
00:33:56,260 --> 00:33:57,280
It's from Sabo!

543
00:33:57,440 --> 00:33:59,337
He must have sent it before he left!

544
00:33:59,420 --> 00:34:01,479
Look, I think it's really from him!

545
00:34:02,140 --> 00:34:02,970
Give it!

546
00:34:03,120 --> 00:34:05,057
Don't worry, I won't head to town.

547
00:34:05,140 --> 00:34:07,022
It's for Luffy and me, isn't it?

548
00:34:13,700 --> 00:34:15,017
Ace! Luffy!

549
00:34:15,100 --> 00:34:17,512
I hope you guys weren't hurt in the fire.

550
00:34:17,720 --> 00:34:21,426
I'm worried about you both, but
something tells me you're okay.

551
00:34:21,660 --> 00:34:23,542
I've got a surprise to tell you.

552
00:34:23,640 --> 00:34:26,880
By the time you get this
letter, I'll be long gone.

553
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:30,480
That's right, I'm heading out to sea.

554
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:35,162
One thing led to another, and I
decided to set out before you two.

555
00:34:40,460 --> 00:34:42,177
I don't know where I'm going yet,

556
00:34:42,260 --> 00:34:45,017
but I do know that anywhere
will be better than this place.

557
00:34:45,100 --> 00:34:47,924
And don't worry, I haven't
given up on my dream.

558
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:49,860
I'm still gonna be a pirate.

559
00:34:50,500 --> 00:34:53,997
I got a head start, but I'm
sure you'll catch up in no time.

560
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:56,760
When we meet again, we'll be unstoppable.

561
00:34:58,620 --> 00:35:00,957
We'll have our reunion on the Grand Line.

562
00:35:01,040 --> 00:35:03,805
Three pirate captains,
more free than the wind.

563
00:35:06,020 --> 00:35:08,440
By the way, Ace, I'm curious.

564
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:12,118
Which one of us do you think
is the real big brother?

565
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:16,809
Anyway, wherever we sail, we'll
always have our brotherhood.

566
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:21,647
It may sound kinda cheesy, but that bond
is what I treasure most in this world.

567
00:35:26,660 --> 00:35:29,477
Luffy is still weak, and a crybaby.

568
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:31,972
Who knows if he'll ever grow out of that.

569
00:35:36,480 --> 00:35:40,640
But he's still our little brother,
so please take good care of him.

570
00:35:41,600 --> 00:35:45,177
G-g-g-g-g
